## Statistics Testing

### Backfill Validation

```powershell
# Run backfill script in dry-run mode first
cd scripts
python backfill_statistics.py --days 7 --dry-run

# Review output before executing
python backfill_statistics.py --days 7 --execute
```

### Energy Dashboard Validation

After statistics changes:

1. **Check for negative values**

   - Energy Dashboard should show no negative kWh
   - Individual sensors should accumulate positively

2. **Verify totals add up**

   ```
   solar_generated = home_consumed + battery_charged + grid_exported + losses
   ```

3. **Compare with source data**
   - Cross-reference with InfluxDB if available
   - Check Tesla app values vs HA values

## Pre-Deployment Checklist

### Configuration Changes

- [ ] YAML syntax validated locally
- [ ] Templates tested in Developer Tools
- [ ] Entity IDs verified to exist
- [ ] Config checked on remote (if possible)
- [ ] Backup of current config saved
- [ ] Rollback plan documented

### Integration Changes

- [ ] Unit tests pass
- [ ] Type checking passes
- [ ] Linter passes (ruff, black, mypy)
- [ ] Integration installs without errors
- [ ] Entities created and updating
- [ ] Logs show no errors

### Automation Changes

- [ ] Conditions tested manually
- [ ] Actions tested in Developer Tools
- [ ] Safety limits in place
- [ ] Trace data looks correct
- [ ] Tested both trigger and non-trigger paths

## Post-Deployment Validation

### Immediate Checks (0-5 minutes)

```powershell
# 1. Check HA container is running
ssh david@192.168.1.110 "docker ps | grep homeassistant"

# 2. Check for errors in logs
ssh david@192.168.1.110 "docker logs --tail 50 homeassistant"

# 3. Verify HA is accessible
# Try accessing http://192.168.1.110:8123
```

### Short-term Checks (5-60 minutes)

- [ ] All sensors updating
- [ ] Automations triggering correctly
- [ ] No error notifications in HA
- [ ] Integrations remain connected
- [ ] Mobile app still works

### Long-term Checks (24 hours)

- [ ] Daily sensors reset correctly at midnight
- [ ] Energy dashboard accumulates properly
- [ ] No unexpected negative values
- [ ] Statistics data continues to flow
- [ ] Battery/solar data matches Tesla app

## Rollback Procedures

### Quick Rollback (Config Changes)

```powershell
# Restore from backup
ssh david@192.168.1.110
sudo cp /opt/homeassistant/config/configuration.yaml.backup \
       /opt/homeassistant/config/configuration.yaml
docker restart homeassistant
```

### Git Rollback

```powershell
# Find the commit to revert
git log --oneline

# Revert specific commit
git revert <commit-hash>

# Or reset to previous commit (careful!)
git reset --hard HEAD~1

# Deploy reverted version
scp homeassistant-config\configuration.yaml david@192.168.1.110:/home/david/
ssh david@192.168.1.110
sudo cp /home/david/configuration.yaml /opt/homeassistant/config/
docker restart homeassistant
```

### Integration Rollback

```powershell
# Remove custom component
ssh david@192.168.1.110
sudo rm -rf /opt/homeassistant/config/custom_components/my_integration/
docker restart homeassistant
```

